The Pitts Special-S models 2 and 3 of the 1930’s were developed in an era when the "light sport" and "midget" categories for powered aerobatic racing had virtually ceased to exist - a situation that was about to turn around rapidly!  Although Pitt's 2nd Special was actually built in the 1936 vintage with a new engine (the "S" in the type name), it was the "Special-S-III" built in 1938 - its "high wing" version - which brought true excitement to powered aerobatics into the late 1940's.  However, the "Light Sport" category soon re-emerged during these war years causing many clubs to re-evaluate their programs in light sportsmanship.  
